dma_pusher: only methods that can write memory move the split's writer mark (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone, and before or after lichii-gpu 0210-0216.

Source: Frizti/Lichii 99b3b49595 (Frizti, branch oot-gather-fix), as narrowed in zortos293/Lichii
cbf7bf99ce (Zortos, perf/frizti-wait-ports; open PR 194 has the same diff as 8f33a1bf4a),
GPL-3.0-or-later.

EDEN_NX2_WRITER_CLASS=1. Before each GP entry the front waits for the last "writer" sent. Today every
compute and copy method the list sends is a writer, so the wait covers all queued work, draws
included. Frizti measured that at about 17% of the front thread in Ocarina on an RTX 4080 PC. That
number does not carry over. Run 61 and 62 cannot say what it is here; lichii-gpu-0210 reports it as
"list writers".

With the switch a native compute method that only stores its value, and a copy register outside the
execution mask, leave the mark. Dispatches, uploads, reports, macros and launches still move it. The
same mark feeds EDEN_NX2_SEM_FAST, EDEN_NX2_DMA_WAIT_WRITERS and EDEN_NX2_LIST_FAST (0215, 0216), so
their waits get shorter too. Frizti notes that with compute always queued such checks almost never
passed before.

Limit: only what the command list sends itself leaves the mark. Frizti's commit blames the QMD fields
macros replay, but with macros on the front those writes never reach the mark, and every macro call
moves it whatever the macro wrote. So a macro that only replays QMD fields moves the mark as before.
The gain is the plain writes a list sends after its last dispatch or macro. Nothing counts those yet,
so the gain here is unknown.

Changed from the source: the call sites stay as they are and a flag tells NoteWriter to leave the
mark, so this applies around 0215's lines; off by default.

Runs on the PS5: yes. Run 61 logs the split with macros on the first thread.
Hang: adds no wait, it only ends one sooner. A plain method cannot write memory by the code:
KeplerCompute::CallMethod stores the value and returns, and those copy registers only reach the method
sink. Lichii's command_writer test checks the same table. One gap: the old mark also covered draws
queued before a plain write, by accident. A list on a page such a draw writes for the first time can
now run stale. The same gap exists today when no compute method follows the draw (0215: "a draw's
first shader store"), and run 62 logged no "written by draws too" line.
Pool memory: none.
Checked: PS5-target syntax compile, alone and on a stack of 42 other patches; anchors unchanged. Not
run.

diff --git a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
index 476077d869..35f3e2a812 100644
--- a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
@@ -455,6 +455,33 @@ bool DmaPusher::WantsSegment() const {
            (engine == Engines::EngineTypes::Maxwell3D && dma_state.method >= MacroRegistersStart);
 }
 
+// EDEN_NX2_WRITER_CLASS=1: a compute or copy method the command list sends moves the split's writer
+// mark only if it can write memory. Without it every one does, so a list fetched after one waits
+// for all work queued before it, draws included. A native plain method only stores its value
+// (KeplerCompute::CallMethod returns right after), and a copy register outside the execution mask
+// only reaches the method sink. Dispatches, uploads, reports and launches still count, and so does
+// every macro call: what a macro writes does not come through here, so one that only replays QMD
+// fields moves the mark as before.
+// From Frizti/Lichii 99b3b49595 (Frizti), as ported in zortos293/Lichii cbf7bf99ce.
+bool DmaPusher::PlainStateMethod() const {
+    static const bool classify = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_WRITER_CLASS");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    if (!classify) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    auto* const engine = subchannels[dma_state.subchannel];
+    switch (subchannel_type[dma_state.subchannel]) {
+    case Engines::EngineTypes::KeplerCompute:
+        return !static_cast<const Engines::KeplerCompute*>(engine)->MayWriteMemory(dma_state.method);
+    case Engines::EngineTypes::MaxwellDMA:
+        return dma_state.method < MacroRegistersStart && !engine->execution_mask[dma_state.method];
+    default:
+        return false;
+    }
+}
+
 void DmaPusher::CallMethod(u32 argument) {
     if (g_semaphore_watch != 0) [[unlikely]] {
         WatchArgument(dma_state.method, argument);
@@ -473,6 +500,7 @@ void DmaPusher::CallMethod(u32 argument) {
             ReportUnboundSubchannel();
             return;
         }
+        split.SetPlainMethod(PlainStateMethod());
         // Compute dispatches and DMA copies write the command lists ReadGpuWrittenCommands reads.
         const auto engine_type = subchannel_type[dma_state.subchannel];
         const bool writer = engine_type == Engines::EngineTypes::KeplerCompute ||
@@ -532,6 +560,7 @@ void DmaPusher::CallMultiMethod(const u32* base_start, u32 num_methods) {
             ReportUnboundSubchannel();
             return;
         }
+        split.SetPlainMethod(PlainStateMethod());
         // Compute dispatches and DMA copies write the command lists ReadGpuWrittenCommands reads.
         const auto engine_type = subchannel_type[dma_state.subchannel];
         const bool writer = engine_type == Engines::EngineTypes::KeplerCompute ||
